course: dictionary
lesson: 9935
title: Tapping: one word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one is meant. Look at the words around it. «Tapping on aquarium glass makes a loud, frightening noise for fish.» Here tapping means hitting something lightly and quickly, again and again, because the sentence is about a noise on glass.
explain: Now read the second sentence: «Tapping on glass, shouting and flash photos frighten animals, which cannot leave as easily as visitors can.» Tapping on glass is still hitting lightly, and the list of frightening things tells you the tapping is causing fear. Try your meaning in the sentence: does hitting lightly and quickly on glass still make sense? Yes, so it fits.
explain: Tapping is a verb form too: tap, taps, tapped, tapping. In a story, a tapping at the window builds suspense, because you hear a quiet, repeated sound and wonder who is there. When you meet tapping, ask: what is happening in this sentence?
fact: Tapping means hitting something lightly and quickly, often again and again, like tapping on a window.
fact: Tapping can also mean touching a phone or tablet screen lightly to choose something.
fact: Tapping a tree means using its sap, and tapping water means using a supply of it.
fact: Phone tapping means secretly listening to someone's phone calls.
fact: A tapping is a noun for a light, repeated knocking sound.
exercise: «Tapping on aquarium glass makes a loud, frightening noise for fish.» What does tapping mean here? | Feeding the fish slowly | *Hitting something lightly and quickly, again and again | Swimming gently past the glass | Cleaning the glass with a cloth
exercise: Lily says tapping on her tablet opens the game. What does tapping mean here? | *Touching the screen lightly to choose something | Listening secretly to calls | Hitting a drum loudly | Turning off the lights
exercise: In music, Sam keeps the beat by tapping his feet. What is he doing? | Singing a loud, long note | Sleeping while the band plays | Running very fast across the stage | *Hitting his feet lightly, again and again, in time
test: In «a tapping at the window», what kind of sound is it? | A song sung softly | A long, silent wait | A loud crash of thunder | *A light, repeated knock
test: Which meaning fits phone tapping? | *Secretly listening to someone's phone calls | Choosing a song by touching the screen | Taking photos of a friend | Charging a phone overnight
exam: Which option uses tapping in the same sense as tapping a tree for sap? | Knocking gently on a door | *Drawing sap out of a tree to use it | Touching a phone screen | Keeping time to music
